# Malawi Food Security GIS System

Automated food price spike detection and 
spatial analysis dashboard for Malawi — 
covering 130 markets across 28 districts, 
January 2020 to present.

## What This Does
- Detects food price spikes using dual-method 
  ALPS methodology (WFP standard)
- Classifies 30 districts by composite risk score
- Serves live GeoJSON via FastAPI to a 
  React-Leaflet web dashboard
- Updates automatically monthly via cron pipeline

## Key Findings (2020–2026)
- Machinga: highest risk district (score: 436)
- 72% of critical events involve maize
- September 2025 post-harvest spike indicates 
  structural supply failure
- Southern Region: 56.7% of all critical events

## Tech Stack
Python · GeoPandas · PostGIS · FastAPI · 
Next.js · React-Leaflet · QGIS · Debian Linux

